\tag{fdip}
\title{Invariant values and group averages}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A finite sum can eliminate a nontrivial group component
without dividing by the group order. The
coefficient of \ref{fdip-00TW} has this property
after contraction of its matter variables as well.
Projection onto all invariant vectors asks for a different
operation and a different hypothesis.}

\transclude{fdip-00WJ}
\transclude{fdip-00WK}
\transclude{fdip-00WL}
